      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Needs maintainer security-boundary review and contributor proof; automation cannot supply the missing real wrapper proof or decide whether to broaden supported command contracts.; Needs attention: The diff changes exec wrapper command identity and currently misclassifies real flock and BSD script operands.; Review finding: [P1] Do not skip -- after the flock lock target — src/infra/dispatch-wrapper-resolution... (sha=5ad14d2c05fd92f2862968e79a8f63013ffc596b)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes dispatch-wrapper parsing for `flock` and BSD `script` separator forms and adds two regression cases for `flock --` wrapper resolution.\n\nPR surface: Source +5, Tests +12. Total +17 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the review findings: the PR diff shows the new reclassification, a live `flock` command failed by trying to execute `--`, and FreeBSD `script` docs/source show the first post-option operand is the transcript file.",
